<title>CANADA: CWB declines comment on China wheat sale rumor.</title>
<headline>CWB declines comment on China wheat sale rumor.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Wheat Board on Monday declined comment on rumors it sold between 0.5 million and 1.5 million tonnes of wheat to China for June-July delivery.</p>
<p>&quot;We neither confirm nor deny there was any sale,&quot; CWB spokesman Jim Pietryk said in an interview.</p>
<p>Trade rumors had the United States selling a cargo load of wheat to China and Canada selling 0.5 to 1.5 million tonnes to China for June-July delivery.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
